cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  RAISR-SME: Auditable Cyber-AI Triage and the Limits of Breach-Based Validation
message: >-
  Anonymous artifact release accompanying the manuscript under peer review.
  Author names, affiliations, and citation details are withheld during review.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Anonymous Authors
    affiliation: Withheld for peer review
url: "https://raisr-sme.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the RAISR-SME v1.0 25-item ternary cyber-AI
  self-assessment checklist and deterministic empirical/simulation audit suite.
  Includes the frozen item bank (bank_v1.json), authoritative NIST CSF 2.0
  subcategory crosswalk and verifier (verify_ids.py), three bit-exact scoring
  engines (Python stdlib, browser JavaScript, and NumPy), automated parity
  tests across 20,006 vectors, retrospective completion-bound and
  boundary-sensitivity audits (retrospective_robustness.py), and four analysis
  suites (exp1 to exp4) auditing UK Cyber Security Breaches Survey (2023 to
  2025) skip-routing and size strata, UK Cyber Security Longitudinal Survey
  (Waves 1 to 4) matched-panel timing and Mundlak models, and 50,000 synthetic
  SME profiles. Licensed UK Data Archive microdata is withheld per End User
  Licence and documented with SHA-256 checksums in DATA.md and data/README.md.
keywords:
  - SME cybersecurity
  - responsible AI
  - formative scoring
  - unknown responses
  - survey measurement
  - synthetic evaluation
license: MIT
version: "2.0.2"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
